# 2026-09-12: all photo/video media (public/assets/img/, public/assets/video/)
# now lives on Vercel Blob, not in the app bundle — see README's "Blob media
# migration" section, and scripts/upload-to-blob.mjs / apply-blob-map.mjs for
# how it got there. These directories are still generated locally by
# scripts/prepare-media.mjs and scripts/prepare-projects-media.mjs (useful
# for reprocessing source material), but nothing in the deployed app reads
# from them any more — every reference in lib/content.ts, lib/about-content.ts
# and lib/generated/projects-media.json points at a Blob URL instead. This is
# also what got the deploy back under the CLI's source-file upload limit
# (100MB Hobby / 1GB Pro) without needing to exclude any page.
/public/assets/img
/public/assets/video

# Standard excludes (this project has no .gitignore fallback quirks, but
# .vercelignore replaces .gitignore entirely once it exists, so repeat them)
/node_modules
/.next
/out
/build
/projects
/assets
